<title>USA: Norfolk Southern motion on Conrail denied.</title>
<headline>Norfolk Southern motion on Conrail denied.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. federal judge Tuesday denied a motion by Norfolk Southern Corp to block a tender offer by CSX Corp for 19.9 percent of Conrail Inc on the grounds that federal disclosure rules had been violated,</p>
<p>The decision preceded rulings by U.S. District Court Judge Donald Van Artsdalen rejecting requests to block a proposed merger between Conrail and CSX on other grounds, including allegations that the deal violated Pennsylvania corporate law.</p>
</text>
